        "question": "A customer misspelled one letter of their name yesterday. Is the correction free?",
        "text": "A one-letter misspelling is a minor correction, which is free if requested within 24 hours of booking [changes#name-corrections]. Since \"yesterday\" may be more than 24 hours after the booking, the exact booking time matters. After 24 hours, the airline's name change rules apply, and many airlines treat any name change as a new ticket [changes#name-corrections]. Advisors can process name corrections, but any change that waives a fee needs supervisor approval [changes#who-can-approve-changes].",
